I am going to the clinic now.
The air after the rain is damp.
Every step feels heavy.
My head has become very heavy.
I put on my light jacket.
And I step out of the house.
It rained a lot during the night.
Because of that, the heat has lessened a bit.
The air outside is cool and damp.
There is a nice smell of wet earth on the street.
But today nothing feels nice to me.
My legs are hurting a lot.
I am walking very slowly down the street.
The clinic is very close to my building.
Usually, it takes only ten minutes to reach there.
But today this road feels very long.
I hold my jacket tightly.
I just want to reach the doctor quickly.
Finally, I see the clinic at the corner of the street.
